DESCRIPTION:Take a deep dive into various topics that have defined Frederick's history\, as we celebrate America's 250th anniversary and our County's role in the Revolution. Featuring brand new exhibits: Cultivating Independence: Frederick in the Revolution Witnessing Revolution All Saints Street: Avenue to the History of Frederick and Its African American Community Growing Gold: A History of Frederick’s Goldfish Industry And returning favorites: Etchison Connections Timeless Toys 24 E Church Street Decorative Arts See our all new and renovated exhibits\, March 7\,2026 through December 12\, 2026. Buy tickets here.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/2026-exhibits-at-museum-of-frederick-county-history/24908/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventqueeraoke25888-20261205@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261112T180609Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261205
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261206
SUMMARY:Queeraoke
DESCRIPTION:Every Second Saturday come and sing your heart out in a safe space in Downtown Frederick! Queeraoke is a karaoke experience like you’ve never had before with your host Black-Eyed Suzy (they/them)\, rolling out games\, challenges\, and sing alongs to keep the vibes flowing. Enjoy the classy drinks from Tenth Ward\, our favorite ally business who knows Pride is 365 days in a year! Let’s support them as they support us in providing a safe space to gather in downtown Frederick. Visit Queeraoke.com to keep up with latest events!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/queeraoke/25888/
END:VEVENT
